message: "If you use pertEvalR, please cite it as below."
title: "pertEvalR: calibrated, signal-aware evaluation of single-cell perturbation response predictions in R"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23431903
date-released: 2026-10-17
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Chaoya
    email: wanchaoya3@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wangchaoya3/pertEvalR"
url: "https://github.com/wangchaoya3/pertEvalR"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - Perturb-seq
  - perturbation prediction
  - virtual cell
  - benchmarking
  - calibration
  - R
abstract: >-
  pertEvalR evaluates models that predict transcriptional responses to
  genetic perturbations from single-cell screens. It diagnoses the signal in
  a dataset (systematic variation, split-half reliability), provides
  leakage-free splits and reference baselines, scores predictions per
  perturbation, compares methods with paired bootstrap intervals and
  signed-rank tests, calibrates scores between an uninformative lower bound
  and a technical-replicate upper bound, and restricts evaluation to reliably
  measured perturbations.
